 "intro": [
  "\"The son of David, the son of Abraham\" (1:1): Matthew arranges the descent in three sets of fourteen. The number may echo the name David, whose Hebrew letters (D-V-D, 4 + 6 + 4) add up to fourteen.",
  "Five women are named: Tamar, Rahab, Ruth, \"Uriah's wife\" and Mary. Several were foreigners, and each story has something irregular about it, preparing for the birth from Mary. The list moves through Solomon and the kings; Luke follows David's son Nathan instead."
 ],
 "countNote": "Matthew counts 14 + 14 + 14, but the third set names only 13 generations. Readers have counted Jeconiah twice, Mary as a generation, or Jesus and \"the Messiah\" separately. Between Joram and Uzziah, Matthew passes over three kings (Ahaziah, Joash and Amaziah).",
 "sources": "Greek names: the Greek text of Matthew; Hebrew forms as in the Hebrew Bible. Babylonian Talmud, Sanhedrin 38a; Rashi. Scholarly summary after the standard commentaries (Davies and Allison; Brown, <i>The Birth of the Messiah</i>).",
